A verb is a word that expresses an action, an occurrence, or a state of being.

examples:

run – She runs every morning.
think – He thinks carefully before answering.
be – They are happy.
write – I write letters to my family.
eat – We eat dinner at 7.
sing – The birds sing at dawn.
build – He built a house.
feel – She feels tired.
go – They go to the park.
know – I know the answer.
